{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Dinner for Four", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Kitchen Tales", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "scholar > Looking to the Stars > Indira Gandhi", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 3, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": " Identify and describe personal and regional eating habits and cooking in a range of communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn6le03ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Expressing quantity with food", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "To talk about specific food quantities and weights the following measures are used throughout North America.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Measurements (Nouns)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Amount\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"pound (lb)<br />  pint (pt)<br /> quart (qt)<br /> ounce (oz)<br />  gallon (gal)<br /> dozen\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a little less than half a kilogram at 454 g<br /> a little less than half a liter<br /> a little less than one liter<br /> almost 30 ml or 30 grams;  8 oz = 250 ml = 1 measuring cup<br /> a little less than 4 liters<br /> 12 pieces\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "In English, we use words we call <span class=\"strong\">quantifiers</span> to talk about undefined quantities. These words are also often used with food. We use different quantifiers depending on whether the noun is <span class=\"strong\">countable</span> or <span class=\"strong\">uncountable</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":5,\"cells\":[\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Large Quantities\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Small Quantities\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Zero Quantities\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"More Than You Need\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Countable</span><br>Lots of (+)<br>Not many (-)<br>How many?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(+) a lot of<br>plenty of\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(a) few<br>very few\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"not ... any<br>none (in short answers)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"too many\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Uncountable</span><br>Lots of (+)<br>Not much (-)<br>How much?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(+) a lot of<br>plenty of\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(a) little<br>very little\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"not ... any<br>none (in short answers)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"too much\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Can you pass me a little salt, please?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I need to boil a few eggs for the spinach salad.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'm full. I ate too much pizza!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I baked plenty of muffins for everyone plus brownies to top off our meal!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I have very little icing left for all these cake layers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You have plenty of room in the sink to drain the fat from the pan.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " What did you use to do?", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " \"<span class=\"strong\">Used to</span>\u201d and \u201c<span class=\"strong\">would</span>\u201d express a pattern of action that occurred regularly in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "But: <br/>Only \"<span class=\"strong\">used to</span>\" expresses repeated habits in the past. <br/>Only \"<span class=\"strong\">would</span>\" is more formal and sentimental.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Structure:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Used to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Would\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject + <span class=\\\"strong\\\">used to</span> + verb in basic form (infinitive) + complement\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject + <span class=\\\"strong\\\">would</span> + verb in basic form (infinitive) + complement\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Examples:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Used to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Would\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"My mom <span class=\\\"strong\\\">used to</span> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">teach</span> me how to cook.<br/>   I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">used to</span> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">spend</span> more time cooking but not anymore.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We <span class=\\\"strong\\\">would</span> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">have</span> lasagna on every holiday.<br/> My grandfather <span class=\\\"strong\\\">would</span> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">read</span> us stories after dinner.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "How did you use to get to school before you got a bicycle?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I used to get up really early to take the bus.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I used to get up early, and I would take my bike out of the locker, put on my helmet, and I would ride all the way to school.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Lasagna used to be a staple in our home.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We used to line the cake trays with wax paper so it wouldn't stick.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "lasagna", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an Italian dish made of ground beef and cheese between layers of pasta noodles ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sally wanted Vanessa to teach her to make lasagna.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le03ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about cooking.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "attention to detail", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to give special care to the details in a task ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: To make a good lasagna requires attention to detail.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le03ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to soak", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make something very wet with water", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You don't have to soak the lasagna noodles in water before cooking.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le03ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "moisture", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a small amount of liquid that makes something wet", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The dry lasagna noodles absorb the moisture from the other ingredients.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le03ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ground beef", "type": "name"}, {"content": "beef that has been ground or broken down to small pieces", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Ground beef is used to make lasagna.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le03ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to spread", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to put something all over a large area", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You usually spread mozzarella cheese over the top of lasagna and pizza. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le03ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Create a recipe for making your favorite pizza. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a list of all the necessary ingredients and the quantities needed in English.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write step-by-step instructions for the preparation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "State the cooking time.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read these instructions to your partner. Ask if the instructions are clear.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I make a list of necessary ingredients for a dish.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I express quantity.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I describe how to prepare food.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read the cooking instructions to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Vocabulary and Grammar", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "I can talk about celebrations and customs.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can describe how to prepare food.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about people's past habits.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Have you ever learned how to cook from a recipe?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, 